8. Session Logic
The app logic must enforce:
SQ-OOP and SSI-OOP separation.
Minimum 2-day gap between OOP questionnaire and OOP interview.
Mandatory break alert at 25 minutes for SQ-OOP.
Time stamping of start, break, pause, resume, end, sync, QA, export.
Skip marking as `S` with reason.
Fatigue and distress flags.
Optional audio recording only when consent exists.
Audio upload, transcription, transcript review, and deletion.
Export block until QA approval and audio deletion.
9. Data Usage and Anonymisation
The data model must protect participants by default. Direct identifiers are stored separately from the research answers. Research outputs should be based on group findings, city-level patterns, stakeholder categories, age bands, and anonymised quotations.
Anonymisation pipeline:
Raw data -> Participant code -> Locked linkage file -> Cleaned instrument data -> De-identified transcript -> QA -> Anonymised export -> Group-level report


Excluded from analysis exports:
Name
Phone
Full address
Signature/thumb impression
Proxy name
Emergency contact
Raw audio
Exact GPS coordinates
Institution actual name without permission
Named official/expert without permission


