Logic.md
CivicAge Survey (CAS) Logic Rules
Project: Smart Cities, Silent Citizens - ICSSR Major Research Project 2025-26
Purpose: Define the rules that control consent, session sequencing, skip logic, timestamping, fatigue safeguards, interviews, FGDs, observations, audio, and QA.
1. Core Logic Idea
The CAS logic layer acts as the ethical and methodological guardrail of the app. It ensures that field investigators cannot accidentally breach protocol by skipping consent, administering the structured questionnaire and interview in one sitting, forgetting the mandatory break, recording audio without consent, retaining audio after transcription, or exporting records before QA approval.
2. Global Session State Machine
NOT_STARTED
  -> CONSENT_REQUIRED
  -> CONSENT_IN_PROGRESS
  -> CONSENT_LOCKED
  -> SESSION_READY
  -> SESSION_IN_PROGRESS
  -> PAUSED
  -> COMPLETED_PENDING_FI_LOG
  -> SUBMITTED_PENDING_SYNC
  -> SYNCED_PENDING_QA
  -> QA_APPROVED
  -> EXPORT_READY


Exception states:
DO_NOT_PROCEED
TERMINATED_EARLY
WITHDRAWN
AUDIO_PENDING_DELETION
QA_EXCLUDED


3. Consent Gate Logic
if (!consent.exists || !consent.locked || consent.consentGiven != true) {
    blockInstrumentStart("Consent is incomplete or not locked.")
}


Consent-to-tool mapping:
Tool group
Required consent
SQ-OOP
OOP written or oral consent.
SSI-OOP
OOP consent plus audio consent if recording.
FO-OOP
Separate shadowing consent.
FGD
Individual consent for every participant.
Expert interviews
Expert/key informant consent.
Institutional tools
Institutional NOC plus individual consent for residents.
Doctrinal template
No human-subject consent; source citation required.


Oral consent rule:
If verbal assent is NO, unclear, confused, or reluctant, set session state to DO_NOT_PROCEED.


Proxy consent rule:
Proxy consent may be recorded only where required by protocol and must not override the participant's clear refusal.


4. SQ vs SSI Separation
val sqDate = getCompletedInstrumentDate(participantCode, "SQ-OOP-v1.0")
val today = currentDate()

if (toolCode == "SSI-OOP-v1.0") {
    require(sqDate != null) { "SQ-OOP must be completed before SSI-OOP." }
    require(daysBetween(sqDate, today) >= 2) { "Minimum 2-day gap from SQ-OOP is required." }
}


Same-day block:
If SQ-OOP is completed today, SSI-OOP button displays: Available after two days.


5. Duration and Break Logic
Tool
Preferred duration
Alert
SQ-OOP
45-55 minutes
Mandatory break at 25 minutes; hard warning near 60 minutes.
SSI-OOP
60-75 minutes
Alert at 60 minutes.
Expert interviews
45-90 minutes
Configurable alert.
Caregiver structured part
15-20 minutes
Alert at 20 minutes.
Caregiver interview
30-40 minutes
Alert at 40 minutes.
Observation
60-120 minutes
Safety check every 30 minutes.
FGD
Protocol based
Moderator-controlled break.


Break trigger:
if (toolCode == "SQ-OOP-v1.0" && elapsedMinutes >= 25 && !breakPromptShown) {
    showBreakPrompt()
    logEvent("break_prompt_shown")
}


6. Skip Logic
Skipped item format:
{
  "questionId": "A7",
  "value": "S",
  "skipReason": "participant_fatigued",
  "skippedAt": 1730000000000,
  "skippedBy": "FI-ND-001"
}


Standard reasons:
participant_refused
participant_fatigued
question_not_applicable
participant_did_not_know
participant_preferred_not_to_say
sensitive_question
language_comprehension_issue
hearing_or_visual_difficulty
time_constraint
fi_protocol_decision


`S - Skipped`, `N/A - Not Applicable`, and `DK - Do Not Know` must be treated as different values.
7. Timestamping Rules
Each session stores:
{
  "createdAt": 1730000000000,
  "startedAt": 1730000000000,
  "breakPromptedAt": 1730001500000,
  "breakStartedAt": 1730001520000,
  "breakEndedAt": 1730001820000,
  "endedAt": 1730003600000,
  "submittedAt": 1730003700000,
  "syncedAt": null,
  "qaReviewedAt": null
}


Offline device timestamps must be reconciled with server timestamps at sync. Large mismatches should be flagged for QA.
8. Fatigue and Distress Logic
Indicators:
confusion
visible tiredness
repeated re-explanation
long silence
emotional distress
hearing difficulty
visual strain
participant asks to pause
participant asks to stop


Rules:
Mild fatigue -> offer break.
Moderate fatigue -> pause or skip non-essential items.
Significant distress -> end sensitive section or terminate session.
Continued distress -> stop session and inform supervisor/PI.


9. Audio Logic
if (audioToggle == true && consent.audioRecordingConsent != true) {
    blockAudioRecording("Audio recording consent has not been given.")
}


Allowed audio rules:
Tool
Audio rule
SQ-OOP
No interview audio; oral assent audio only if required.
SSI-OOP
Optional with consent.
Expert interviews
Optional with consent.
Caregiver interview
Optional with consent.
FGD
Only if all participants consent.
Observation
Ambient only if separately consented; no photography without specific consent.


Audio states:
not_started -> recording_local -> uploaded_temp -> transcribing -> transcribed -> transcript_reviewed -> audio_deleted


10. Flow by Instrument
SQ-OOP
Consent locked -> metadata -> Sections A to C -> 25-minute break -> Sections D to G -> FI Section H -> review skips -> submit


SSI-OOP
Verify 2-day gap -> confirm consent/audio -> pre-interview checklist -> themes T1-T5 -> 60-minute alert -> closing -> reflexivity log -> transcript if audio -> QA


FGD
